<p>Warner Bros. Discovery says it’s ready to talk with Paramount after Paramount raised its all-cash offer to $31 per share, keeping the race for the studio alive as Netflix weighs its own next move, according to reporting across the outlets. Semafor reported the bidding is becoming increasingly tied up in U.S. politics, with President Trump and lawmakers adding pressure that could shape the path to approval.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/E73e65HlBOOdfHkItdRohrvJ7B7lkXhsuA7xrQuJ5wXVKd1U4-y82iUDVYlPzpNPankyrBoafvHX3rSEcotbS8Voz1hA0YXZJHbmIYtq5Lewok9pL0hf_ESwnQN_i6j1HPQEMho-ruyZ-E-deN0Z3KlwfVoJ1WqebywHFYhV7CuhQEKzkA' alt='An aerial view of the Paramount logo on the water tower at Paramount Studios in Los Angeles, California, Feb. 23, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Warner’s stance: The company says it’s willing to engage after Paramount sweetened its all-cash proposal.</li><li>Semafor’s read: Semafor reported it has heard David Ellison’s new offer goes beyond the $31 starting point, putting him back in the mix.</li><li>Netflix in the spotlight: Semafor described Ellison’s move as forcing Netflix to either raise its bid or defend a more complex agreement to buy Warner and its franchise-rich library.</li><li>White House attention: Semafor said Trump has targeted a Netflix board member and wants Warner-owned CNN “neutered”.</li></ul><blockquote>This is a business deal, it’s not a political deal - Ted Sarandos</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Warner Bros. Discovery: The company says it’s prepared to engage with Paramount after Paramount improved the terms of its cash proposal. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/culture/article/2026/02/25/warner-bros-opens-door-to-paramount-as-bidding-war-continues-to-heat-up_6750848_30.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Paramount (David Ellison bid): Semafor reported that Paramount is leaning on “politics,” as well as price, as it tries to improve its position in the race for Warner Bros. Discovery. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/24/2026/paramount-launches-new-higher-offer-into-warner-bros'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Netflix leadership: Semafor reported Netflix co-CEO Ted Sarandos cast the contest as a business decision and waved off Trump’s remarks as “social-media noise”. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/24/2026/paramount-launches-new-higher-offer-into-warner-bros'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>U.S. lawmakers: Semafor reported that Senate Republicans want to see Netflix “humbled,” while Senate Democrats want to make Ellison the face of influence-peddling in Washington. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/24/2026/paramount-launches-new-higher-offer-into-warner-bros'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/culture/article/2026/02/25/warner-bros-opens-door-to-paramount-as-bidding-war-continues-to-heat-up_6750848_30.html'>Warner Bros opens door to Paramount as bidding war continues to heat up</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/warner-bros-opens-door-to-paramount-after-higher-offer/'>Warner Bros opens door to Paramount after higher offer</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/24/2026/paramount-launches-new-higher-offer-into-warner-bros'>Paramount bets that politics, price will win it Warner Bros.</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/warner-bros-opens-door-to-paramount-as-bidding-war-heats-up/article70673109.ece'>Warner Bros. opens door to Paramount as bidding war heats up</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>